The render corpus: 28 pages (ADR 033 (a)), rendered by `cargo xtask render` and
compared exactly with tests/render/baselines/<id>.png. Listed in pages.toml.

Text paints as Ahem glyphs (Phase 9); the text baselines were re-blessed in one
reviewed `cargo xtask render --bless` commit.

16 hand-written feature fixtures: tests/render/pages/*.html, one idea each.

12 pages derived from the vendored WPT corpus (pinned commit
b875b21fd9e6b688e37c10d1b6366cab7418f91e, see tests/wpt/*/PROVENANCE). They are used
in place, not copied: pages.toml names the test and its reference, and the gate
asserts they render to identical bytes (a pixel-level reftest).

Selection rule (implemented as `select_every_kth` and `pair_eligible` in
crates/px-xtask/src/gates/render.rs, reproduced by `cargo xtask render --select`):

  1. Per suite, list every file carrying exactly one <link rel="match"> whose
     target exists, in sorted path order.
  2. Keep the pairs whose test and reference both render and produce byte-identical
     PNGs, and whose bitmap has at least 400 ink pixels (pixels differing from its
     most common colour). A page that paints one flat colour is not a test.
  3. With n eligible pairs and quota q, k = n / q (at least 1); take the pairs at
     positions 0, k, 2k, ... until q are taken.

Nothing was chosen by how a page looks. Quotas: css2 6, css-flexbox 3, css-grid 3.

