Known limits: several of these reference inline-box backgrounds or features the
display-list builder does not paint yet (no inline-box backgrounds, no stacking
contexts). The rule was applied as stated and not adjusted, so a chosen page may
paint less than its CSS asks for; the test and reference agree anyway. The
selection is a record of one run of the rule: re-running `--select` after layout or
paint changes may choose differently, and doing so is a deliberate corpus change.

Canvas: 800 px wide, max(600, document height) tall, capped at 2400.

8 pages (ui-page-*): the browser's built-in pages from crates/px-pages/pages/,
each in the light and the dark scheme (a `#dark` suffix on the source renders with
prefers-color-scheme: dark). They are used in place, not copied. PNG copies for
review are in docs/brand/ui-page-*.png.

8 pages (table-*): hand-written table fixtures (basic, spans, widths, collapsed
borders, vertical-align and captions, anonymous boxes, spacing and empty-cells,
legacy attributes). Each baseline was viewed before it was committed.
